Chapter: GopCal
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Layout
  cites UI chapter Theme

 The calendar, moved out of `apps/guios/CalendarApp.codex` when the guios
 shell retired into GopDesk. The date arithmetic is that chapter's,
 unchanged.

 What changed is the rendering. The old one laid out a two-row header as
 widgets and then placed all 28 to 31 day numbers itself with hand-computed
 pixel positions into a GopBuf. Here the whole month is a widget tree: six
 rows of seven cells, laid out by the same flex engine as everything else,
 so the grid divides the pane's real width instead of a `(win-w - 32) / 7`
 the caller had to get right.

 **Today is a button and every other day is a label.** That is the whole
 highlight mechanism, and it is deliberate: a button paints its background
 from the theme and a label does not, so the current day stands out using
 only the two widget kinds `GopComposite` already draws. The old chapter
 filled a rectangle behind the number itself, which is a thing a pane
 cannot do when it hands back a tree rather than a buffer.

 This chapter reads no clock. The RTC is a port device and reading it is
 an effect; GopDesk already owns `rtc-read` and passes the date in, so the
 tree stays pure and the same three numbers can be handed in by a test.

Section: Date Math

 The proleptic Gregorian rules, all three of them, because a calendar that
 is right for the next three years and wrong in 2100 is worse than one that
 is obviously wrong now.

  gcal-is-leap : Integer -> Boolean
  gcal-is-leap (y) =
    if int-mod y 400 == 0 then True
    else if int-mod y 100 == 0 then False
    else int-mod y 4 == 0

  gcal-days-in-month : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gcal-days-in-month (m) (y) =
    if m == 2 then (if gcal-is-leap y then 29 else 28)
    else if m == 4 then 30
    else if m == 6 then 30
    else if m == 9 then 30
    else if m == 11 then 30
    else 31

 Day of week for 1 January, counting from Sunday = 0. The + 1 is the
 anchor: 1 January year 1 was a Monday in the proleptic calendar.

  gcal-dow-jan1 : Integer -> Integer
  gcal-dow-jan1 (y) =
    let y1 = y - 1
    in int-mod (1 + y1 + y1 / 4 - y1 / 100 + y1 / 400) 7

  gcal-dow-offset : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gcal-dow-offset (dow) (cm) (target-m) (y) =
    if cm >= target-m then dow
    else gcal-dow-offset (int-mod (dow + gcal-days-in-month cm y) 7) (cm + 1) target-m y

  gcal-dow-month1 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gcal-dow-month1 (m) (y) = gcal-dow-offset (gcal-dow-jan1 y) 1 m y

  gcal-month-name : Integer -> Text
  gcal-month-name (m) =
    if m == 1 then "January"
    else if m == 2 then "February"
    else if m == 3 then "March"
    else if m == 4 then "April"
    else if m == 5 then "May"
    else if m == 6 then "June"
    else if m == 7 then "July"
    else if m == 8 then "August"
    else if m == 9 then "September"
    else if m == 10 then "October"
    else if m == 11 then "November"
    else "December"

Section: Grid

 A cell is addressed by its position in the six-by-seven grid, and the day
 it carries is `pos - dow1 + 1`. Positions before the first of the month
 and past the last carry a blank label rather than being absent, so every
 row has seven children and the columns line up under the weekday header.

  gcal-pad : Integer -> Text
  gcal-pad (d) = if d < 10 then " " & show d else show d

  gcal-cell : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  gcal-cell (pos) (dow1) (days) (today) =
    let d = pos - dow1 + 1
    in if d < 1 then widget-set-flex (widget-label ("gcal-b" & show pos) "  ") 1
    else if d > days then widget-set-flex (widget-label ("gcal-b" & show pos) "  ") 1
    else if d == today then widget-set-flex (widget-set-min (widget-button ("gcal-t" & show pos) (gcal-pad d)) 0 20) 1
    else widget-set-flex (widget-label ("gcal-d" & show pos) (gcal-pad d)) 1

  gcal-week : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  gcal-week (w) (dow1) (days) (today) =
    let p = w * 7
    in widget-panel ("gcal-w" & show w) DirRow 2 [
      gcal-cell p dow1 days today,
      gcal-cell (p + 1) dow1 days today,
      gcal-cell (p + 2) dow1 days today,
      gcal-cell (p + 3) dow1 days today,
      gcal-cell (p + 4) dow1 days today,
      gcal-cell (p + 5) dow1 days today,
      gcal-cell (p + 6) dow1 days today
    ]

 Six rows always. A month can start on a Saturday and run 31 days, which
 needs 6 rows; drawing only the rows a given month fills would make the
 pane change height from month to month.

  gcal-dow-header : Integer -> WidgetNode
  gcal-dow-header (dummy) =
    widget-panel "gcal-dh" DirRow 2 [
      widget-set-flex (widget-label "gcal-h0" "Su") 1,
      widget-set-flex (widget-label "gcal-h1" "Mo") 1,
      widget-set-flex (widget-label "gcal-h2" "Tu") 1,
      widget-set-flex (widget-label "gcal-h3" "We") 1,
      widget-set-flex (widget-label "gcal-h4" "Th") 1,
      widget-set-flex (widget-label "gcal-h5" "Fr") 1,
      widget-set-flex (widget-label "gcal-h6" "Sa") 1
    ]

  gcal-tree : Integer, Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  gcal-tree (year) (month) (today) =
    let days = gcal-days-in-month month year
    in let dow1 = gcal-dow-month1 month year
    in widget-panel "gcal-root" DirColumn 6 [
      widget-label "gcal-title" (gcal-month-name month & " " & show year),
      widget-separator "gcal-sep",
      gcal-dow-header 0,
      gcal-week 0 dow1 days today,
      gcal-week 1 dow1 days today,
      gcal-week 2 dow1 days today,
      gcal-week 3 dow1 days today,
      gcal-week 4 dow1 days today,
      gcal-week 5 dow1 days today,
      widget-separator "gcal-sep2",
      widget-label "gcal-help" "Esc returns."
    ]
